From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:09:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 142/151] Find: In selection stays inside the selection;
 closing the bar ends it; Ctrl+F3 updates the count

- A Replace that finds nothing left in the range no longer counts as an
  edit, so "In selection" stays on and the next Replace stays inside it.
- A range that no longer holds (an edit, another tab) is no scope at all:
  find, replace, replace all, the count and the highlights act on nothing
  and the option shows off, until it is turned on again or the bar closes.
  It never silently widens to the whole file.
- Every way the find bar closes (Escape, Go to line, the preview-only
  Markdown view, the close button) ends "In selection", so F3 never cycles
  inside a range that is not shown.
- Opening the bar sets the range from the selection only when the bar was
  closed, and never from the match the last find selected (Ctrl+H after
  Find next).
- Ctrl+F3 compiles and counts the new query, so the count and highlights
  follow it.
- A Vi mode change that leaves the text as it was no longer counts as an
  edit (it only refreshes the status bar).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

